{"duration_api_ms":120578,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"3c857c81-ace5-4cbc-9339-36ed91eeef0d","total_cost_usd":0.7017490000000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":44,"cache_creation_input_tokens":44869,"cache_read_input_tokens":788005,"output_tokens":9251,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1917},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":44869,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":731,"cache_read_input_tokens":49839,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1010,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1010},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":44,"outputTokens":9251,"cacheReadInputTokens":788005,"cacheCreationInputTokens":44869,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7017490000000002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1917,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01YTdvMNedGX4iYgek4PNQvM","tool_input":{"command":"cd /Users/christoph/Privat/samples/wp68-java; ls src/test-integration/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/product/; cat src/test-integration/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/product/ProductCatalogPageIntegrationTest.java; for f in tasks/CAT-01/breaks/*.patch; do echo \"--- $f\"; cat \"$f\"; git apply --check \"$f\" && echo APPLIES; done","description":"Show integration test and check break patches apply"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01NMho6UtSYXj4HX3FsnQ6Zk","tool_input":{"command":"git apply --check -v tasks/CAT-01/breaks/*.patch","description":"Check that the break patches apply cleanly"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01XqxqgzyAtkdbXXsMi6R2uG","tool_input":{"command":"cd /Users/christoph/Privat/samples/wp68-java && for f in tasks/CAT-01/breaks/*.patch; do patch -p1 --dry-run < \"$f\"; done","description":"Dry-run the break patches against the working tree"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01SXxnXDxBVSiyWWGMjRojnB","tool_input":{"command":"cd /Users/christoph/Privat/samples/wp68-java && patch -p1 --dry-run < tasks/CAT-01/breaks/ProductCatalogPageIntegrationTest--listsTheCardTitlesInOrdinalNameOrder.patch && patch -p1 --dry-run < tasks/CAT-01/breaks/ProductCatalogPageIntegrationTest--cardShowsTheProductsNameDescriptionAndImage.patch && patch -p1 --dry-run < tasks/CAT-01/breaks/ProductCatalogPageIntegrationTest--everyCardOffersAViewDetailsLinkToThatProductsPage.patch && patch -p1 --dry-run < tasks/CAT-01/breaks/ProductCatalogPageIntegrationTest--pageIsTitledHeadedAndPlacedAsTheCatalogue.patch","description":"Dry-run the break patches against the working tree"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01GeZf4fehF3UFS52wBo45tH","tool_input":{"command":"cd /Users/christoph/Privat/samples/wp68-java && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport glob, re\nfor path in sorted(glob.glob(\"tasks/CAT-01/breaks/*.patch\")):\n    lines = open(path).read().split(\"\\n\")\n    if lines and lines[-1] == \"\": lines = lines[:-1]\n    out, in_hunk, target = [], False, None\n    for l in lines:\n        if l.startswith(\"+++ b/\"): target = l[6:]; in_hunk = False\n        elif l.startswith(\"@@\"): in_hunk = True\n        elif l.startswith(\"diff --git\"): in_hunk = False\n        if in_hunk and l == \"\": l = \" \"\n        out.append(l)\n    open(path, \"w\").write(\"\\n\".join(out) + \"\\n\")\n    # verify every hunk's old side matches the file at its start line\n    src = open(target).read().split(\"\\n\")\n    ok = True\n    hunks = [i for i, l in enumerate(out) if l.startswith(\"@@\")]\n    for h in hunks:\n        m = re.match(r\"@@ -(\\d+),(\\d+) \\+(\\d+),(\\d+) @@\", out[h])\n        start, n_old, _, n_new = map(int, m.groups())\n        body = []\n        for l in out[h+1:]:\n            if l.startswith(\"@@\") or l.startswith(\"diff --git\"): break\n            body.append(l)\n        old = [l[1:] for l in body if l[0] in \" -\"]\n        new = [l[1:] for l in body if l[0] in \" +\"]\n        ok &= len(old) == n_old and len(new) == n_new and src[start-1:start-1+n_old] == old\n    print(\"OK \" if ok else \"BAD\", path)\nEOF","description":"Normalise blank context lines in break patches and verify hunks"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01YTd3z8aDLBvM67xmUJBCdZ","tool_input":{"command":"cd /Users/christoph/Privat/samples/wp68-java && ./gradlew testClasses test-integration --rerun --tests \"*ProductCatalogPageIntegrationTest*\" -q 2>&1 | tail -30; echo \"exit: $?\"","timeout":600000,"description":"Compile and run the catalogue page integration tests"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":34,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The test stage for CAT-01 is finished. This was a second round: a first round had already written the tests and `tasks/CAT-01/tests.md`, so this round re-checked them on the current code. I wrote no new tests.\n\n**What the gate reads** (`tasks/CAT-01/tests.md`, the criterion-to-test table):\n- **catalogue-lists-the-seeded-range** (the happy path) maps to the existing `SeededCatalogE2ETest#catalogListsTheSeededProductsInNameOrder`. It passes: `./gradlew test-e2e --rerun --tests \"*SeededCatalogE2ETest*\"` succeeded.\n- **The other four criteria** map to `ProductCatalogPageIntegrationTest`. These are characterization tests (tests that pin down how today's code behaves), and all four pass on today's code (4 tests, 0 failures).\n\n**Breaks** (one patch per characterization test that should make just that test fail):\n- I made the four changes by hand in the working tree and ran the class. All 4 tests failed, each on its own assertion:\n  - the reversed sort order;\n  - an empty description (`\"\"`);\n  - the link label reading \"View\" instead of \"View Details\";\n  - the heading reading \"Products\" instead of \"Our Products\".\n- I then reverted them. `git status --short src/main` is empty and the class passes again.\n- The patch files themselves have not been run through a patch tool. `git apply --check`, `patch --dry-run` and `python3` all needed approval here. Instead I compared every hunk by hand against the current `InMemoryProductRepository.java` and `catalog.pug`, and they match line for line.\n- The blank context lines in the patches are stored as empty lines rather than a single space. I believe `git apply` accepts that, but it hasn't been tried. If the gate refuses a patch, that is the likely cause.\n\nI ran `spotlessApply` last. The only change to `tests.md` is the round-2 notes above; the table and file list are unchanged. I changed no production code, no existing test and no build file, and ran no other stage.","ttft_ms":4644,"type":"result","duration_ms":184034,"uuid":"ea23fdcb-e84e-4ecc-81d2-747b35f57d9c","ttft_stream_ms":3324,"time_to_request_ms":71,"first_content_frame_ms":3324,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
